# .publishignore — dev-only paths to keep OUT of the public repo.
#
# Used by publish.sh as `rsync --exclude-from`. Patterns are relative to each
# published path (see PUBLISH_PATHS in publish.sh) and use rsync filter syntax,
# which is close to .gitignore:
#   - trailing slash matches directories:      scratch/
#   - leading slash anchors to the path root:  /experimental.py
#   - glob:                                    *_wip.py
#
# Currently empty: all dev-only files (analyze_overlap.py, configs/, notes/,
# tests/, etc.) live at the repo ROOT, outside the published doolyprof/ package,
# so they are never copied. Add patterns here only if you introduce dev-only
# files INSIDE doolyprof/ that should not be published.
*.bak